{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מורשה", :translit "morashah", :gloss "heritage"} {:he "מורשה קהלת יעקב", :translit "morashah kehillat ya'akov", :gloss "the assembly of Jacob, a heritage"} {:he "ונתתי אותה לכם מורשה", :translit "venatati otah lakhem morashah", :gloss "and I will give it to you as a heritage"} {:he "ויתן להם ארצות גוים", :translit "vayiten lahem aratzot goyim", :gloss "and He gave them lands of nations"} {:he "בעבור ישמרו חקיו ותורותיו ינצורו", :translit "ba'avur yishmeru chukav vetorotav yintzoru", :gloss "so that they would observe His statutes and guard His teachings"} {:he "התורה אינה ירושה לך", :translit "hatorah einah yerushah lakh", :gloss "the Torah is not an inheritance to you"} {:he "מורשה, ולא ירושה", :translit "morashah, v'lo yerushah", :gloss "heritage, and not inheritance"} {:he "קהלת יעקב", :translit "kehillat ya'akov", :gloss "assembly of Jacob"} {:he "איש תם יושב אוהלים", :translit "ish tam yoshev ohalim", :gloss "a wholesome man, dwelling in tents"} {:he "מה טובו אוהליך יעקב", :translit "mah tovu ohalekha ya'akov", :gloss "how goodly are your tents, O Jacob"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מורשה קהלת יעקב" "ונתתי אותה לכם מורשה"]} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: מורשה (heritage) contrasted with ירושה (inheritance) — heritage is not automatically possessed."}], :frame {:text "The Sages interpret Leviticus 25:38, where God says 'I will give it to you as a heritage (מורשה),' to mean the Torah is a morashah, not a yerushah — a heritage available to all who labor for it, not an automatic possession passed down (Tractate Eruvin 54a, in some versions: Nedarim 55a). The phrase איש תם יושב אוהלים describes Jacob at Genesis 25:27, understood midrashically as Jacob's constant presence in the tents of Torah study (Bereshit Rabbah 63:10). Balaam's blessing מה טובו אוהליך יעקב at Numbers 24:5 is likewise read as praise of the tents of Torah and the synagogues and study halls of Israel. By linking מורשה קהלת יעקב to these verses, Ba'al HaTurim teaches that Torah endures specifically when the assembly of Jacob gathers in those tents of study.", :sources ["Leviticus 25:38" "Eruvin 54a" "Genesis 25:27" "Bereshit Rabbah 63:10" "Numbers 24:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מורשה קהלת יעקב" "ונתתי אותה לכם מורשה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מורשה קהלת יעקב", :refs ["Deuteronomy 33:4"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ונתתי אותה לכם מורשה", :refs ["Exodus 6:8"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: מורשה (heritage) contrasted with ירושה (inheritance) — heritage is not automatically possessed.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:41:22.179305588Z", :model "glm-5.2"}